{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2282","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2282","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2282\",\"parent_revision\":\"ccc795d1d66e26d9473998bf82e78459193a9167608e30f4d330c46a7b6d3391\",\"root_revision\":\"ccc795d1d66e26d9473998bf82e78459193a9167608e30f4d330c46a7b6d3391\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe implement-feature skill documents the dispatch loop, concern collection, contract verification, and shutdown sequencing \u2014 but contains no documentation of git commit responsibility.\\n\\nDuring execution of Pdec8934d, agents T22, T26, and T28 completed their tasks and reported STATUS: COMPLETE without committing their changes. The orchestrator had no documented rule governing this situation and inferred behaviour inconsistently.\\n\\nTwo execution modes exist today but neither has documented commit ownership:\\n\\n1. Same worktree (default, no isolation flag): Multiple agents write to the same filesystem concurrently. An agent committing mid-task risks including another agent's in-progress changes. The orchestrator receives each completion message serially and is the only actor with a safe, serialised view of which files belong to which completed task.\\n\\n2. Isolated worktree (worktree isolation variant, routes to work-milestone): Each agent has its own worktree. The agent can commit safely as it goes. The orchestrator merges each worktree back when the completion message arrives.\\n\\nNeither rule is written down anywhere in the skill. This creates inconsistent behaviour across runs and agents \u2014 some agents commit, some do not, and the orchestrator has no instruction for either case.\\n\\nThe fix must document both rules explicitly in implement-feature/SKILL.md so every orchestrator invocation produces a consistent git history regardless of which agents chose to commit or not commit during their task.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n\\nAll required inputs are present or derivable from primary sources.\\n\\n- Functional intent: PRESENT \u2014 add commit ownership rules to `implement-feature/SKILL.md` for both same-worktree and isolated-worktree dispatch modes\\n- Scope boundaries: PRESENT \u2014 file identified at the installed plugin cache path; scope is documentation-only, no code changes\\n- External interfaces: PRESENT \u2014 git commit semantics; orchestrator dispatch loop documented in the skill file; `start-task/SKILL.md` step 6 has `Fixes #N` prohibition but no ownership rules for the orchestrator\\n- Constraints: PRESENT \u2014 rule must distinguish same-worktree from isolated-worktree; orchestrator owns commits in same-worktree; agent owns commits in isolated-worktree\\n- Existing system context: PRESENT \u2014 verified grep shows no commit ownership documentation exists in `implement-feature/SKILL.md`; `start-task/SKILL.md` step 6 is the closest prior art (commit trailer restriction, not ownership rule)\\n- Verification expectations: DERIVABLE \u2014 grep for commit-ownership text in file after change; observable behavior in subsequent runs when agents complete tasks without committing\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **implement-feature skill missing commit ownership documentation for same-worktree vs isolated-worktree execution** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed during /dh:implement-feature Pdec8934d \u2014 agents T22, T26, T28 completed tasks without committing; orchestrator had no documented rule for what to do. Confirmed by grep: implement-feature/SKILL.md has no commit ownership documentation.\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-16)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n\\nAll required inputs are present. No blockers. Ready for implementation.\\n\\n- Functional intent: PRESENT \u2014 add commit ownership rules to `implement-feature/SKILL.md` for both same-worktree and isolated-worktree dispatch modes\\n- Scope boundaries: PRESENT \u2014 file confirmed at `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md`; scope is documentation-only, no code changes required\\n- External interfaces: PRESENT \u2014 git commit semantics; orchestrator dispatch loop at lines 35\u2013265 of SKILL.md; `start-task/SKILL.md` line 159 documents the `Fixes #N` trailer prohibition (cross-reference target)\\n- Constraints: PRESENT \u2014 rule must distinguish same-worktree (orchestrator commits after step 4b) from isolated-worktree (agent commits in own worktree, orchestrator merges via work-milestone)\\n- Existing system context: PRESENT \u2014 grep confirms only one `commit` mention in `implement-feature/SKILL.md` (line 124, health-check context), confirming no commit ownership documentation exists; insertion point confirmed at lines 220\u2013244 (between step 4b and the per-task confirmation gate)\\n- Verification expectations: DERIVABLE \u2014 `grep -i 'commit' plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` returns results referencing both execution modes; `uv run prek run --files` exits 0\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n10/10 \u2014 P0 Bug. Produces non-deterministic git history on every implement-feature run. Agents T22, T26, and T28 from plan Pdec8934d completed work without committing; the orchestrator had no documented rule to apply. Every future same-worktree dispatch run is subject to the same ambiguity until this is fixed.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: reliable SAM implement-feature execution \u2014 any plan run in same-worktree mode may produce uncommitted or partially-committed work after agent completion\\n- Bottleneck: every orchestrator invocation that reaches task completion has no defined commit ownership rule, forcing inconsistent ad-hoc inference\\n- Scope: all implement-feature skill consumers (the orchestrator) and all dh:task-worker agents dispatched from it\\n- Related: #2283 (swarm-task-planner must generate commit step in task acceptance criteria) \u2014 companion item addressing the same root incident from the planner side; can proceed in parallel\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Eliminates non-deterministic git history after implement-feature runs\\n- Gives the orchestrator an explicit, documented rule to apply when agents complete without committing\\n- Prevents orphaned changes from requiring manual discovery and commit after each wave\\n- Consistent behavior across full_auto, checkpoint, and per_task autonomy modes\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen an agent completes a task in same-worktree mode, the orchestrator (not the agent) is responsible for committing that agent's changes before dispatching the next batch. In isolated-worktree mode (routed via work-milestone), each agent commits in its own worktree; the orchestrator merges on completion receipt and no orchestrator-level commit step is needed.\\n\\nThe documented rule makes responsibility explicit and observable: after a task completion message is received in same-worktree mode, the orchestrator inspects `git status`, attributes unstaged changes to the completed task, and commits them with a message referencing the task ID \u2014 before dispatching the next task.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe `implement-feature/SKILL.md` file contains a new section \u2014 'Commit Ownership' or equivalent \u2014 that:\\n\\n1. States which actor owns commits in same-worktree mode (the orchestrator, after step 4b)\\n2. States which actor owns commits in isolated-worktree mode (the agent; orchestrator merges via work-milestone)\\n3. Specifies what to commit (files modified by the just-completed task, identified via `git status` or `git diff HEAD`)\\n4. Specifies when to commit (after concerns collection and contract verification in step 4, before dispatching the next task)\\n5. Cross-references the `Fixes #N` prohibition from `start-task/SKILL.md` line 159 so orchestrator-level commits also comply\\n\\nPlacement: between step 4b (shutdown completed teammate) and step 5 (fetch next batch status) in the Progress Loop \u2014 the natural location where the orchestrator has a serialised view of completed work.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -i 'commit' plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` returns at least one result that covers commit ownership for both execution modes\\n2. The documented rule specifies the orchestrator as commit owner in same-worktree mode (after step 4b, before dispatching the next task)\\n3. The documented rule specifies the agent as commit owner in isolated-worktree mode (via work-milestone); orchestrator does not commit\\n4. The commit timing is documented relative to the existing steps (steps 4\u20134b) in the Progress Loop\\n5. The `Fixes #N` trailer prohibition from `start-task/SKILL.md` line 159 is referenced or echoed so orchestrator-level commits also comply\\n6. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` exits 0\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:implement-feature \u2014 file to modify: `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` |\\n| Skill | /dh:start-task \u2014 line 159: `Fixes #N` trailer prohibition (cross-reference target for orchestrator commits) |\\n| Skill | /dh:work-milestone \u2014 isolated-worktree path; agents commit independently before orchestrator merges |\\n| Skill | /dh:complete-implementation \u2014 Final Step documents the post-all-tasks commit-and-push pattern |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` lines 210\u2013244 \u2014 steps 4b and 5 bracket the insertion point |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` line 159 \u2014 commit message restriction to cross-reference |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 all inputs present; target file and insertion point confirmed\\n- Blocks: #2283 (swarm-task-planner must generate commit step in task acceptance criteria) \u2014 complementary gap on the planner side; both items can proceed in parallel\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 documentation-only change to a single SKILL.md file. The rules are fully described in the item description. The insertion point (between steps 4b and 5 in the Progress Loop, lines 210\u2013244) is confirmed. No code changes, no tests, no schema changes required. Estimated 30\u201360 minutes including linting.\\n\",\"digest\":\"99e096ba324cd2124e21009eed5d474a83585ef5bca0cf136bc35da01a5e79fe\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCRDmQ\"}"}